WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:08.070
I have seen APC today. He is a very pleasant gentleman who is 42 years old, 344 pounds.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:39.210
He is 59. He has BMA of 51. He has been overweight for 10 years since the age of 33. At his highest, he was 358 pounds. At his lowest, 260. He is pursuing surgical attempts of weight loss to feel good, get healthy and begin to exercise again. He wants to be able to exercise and play volleyball. Physically, he is sluggish. He gets tired quickly. He doesn't go out often.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:01:40.070
When he loses weight, he always regains it and he gains back more than he lost. His biggest weight loss is 25 pounds and it was 3 months before he gained it back. He did 6 months of not drinking alcohol and not taking in many calories. He has been on multiple commercial weight loss programs including SlimFast for 1 month, 1 year ago and Atkins diet for 1 month, 2 years ago. Past medical history. He has difficulty climbing stairs, difficulty with airline seats, tying shoes, using public seating, difficulty walking, high cholesterol and high blood pressure. He has asthma and difficulty walking 2 blocks or going 8 to 10 steps. He has sleep apnea and snoring. He is diabetic on medication. He has joint pain, knee pain, back pain, foot and ankle pain, leg and foot swelling.
